WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:38.977
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:39.247 --> 00:42.959
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:43.042 --> 00:45.670
‎THIS DRAMA IS FICTITIOUS AND DIFFERS FROM ‎ACTUAL MEDICAL PRACTICES AND REGULATIONS.

4
00:45.754 --> 00:47.964
‎CHARACTERS AND SETTINGS ARE FICTIONAL. ‎CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED SAFELY.

5
01:00.769 --> 01:02.937
‎-Aunt. ‎-I'm fine. Hurry.

6
01:11.362 --> 01:12.322
‎Aunt.

7
01:12.405 --> 01:13.948
‎-I-- ‎-Save the patient.

8
01:15.033 --> 01:15.867
‎Hurry and operate.

9
01:16.743 --> 01:17.577
‎Su-jeong.

10
01:18.495 --> 01:19.662
‎You can do this.

11
01:59.828 --> 02:00.662
‎Aunt.

12
02:01.329 --> 02:05.208
‎You promised to teach me how to do ‎a multi-organ transplant for graduation.

13
02:05.708 --> 02:07.418
‎A solo surgery, no less.

14
02:08.378 --> 02:10.046
‎Tell me what you said to me that day.

15
02:12.257 --> 02:13.383
‎There's no one else.

16
02:14.551 --> 02:16.136
‎It's just you.

17
02:18.304 --> 02:20.306
‎You won't always have

18
02:20.849 --> 02:23.309
‎a primary surgeon, assistant,

19
02:24.144 --> 02:27.230
‎anesthesiologist, circulator,

20
02:28.064 --> 02:30.400
‎and scrub nurse for every surgery.

21
02:32.235 --> 02:33.194
‎A doctor

22
02:34.529 --> 02:35.780
‎never leaves

23
02:36.948 --> 02:38.491
‎their patient's side.

24
02:40.994 --> 02:42.745
‎It's their obligation.

25
02:45.874 --> 02:46.791
‎That's why

26
02:48.042 --> 02:50.003
‎we became doctors.

27
02:51.296 --> 02:52.839
‎What else?

28
02:53.673 --> 02:55.216
‎Aunt, keep talking.

29
02:56.009 --> 02:57.093
‎Don't fall asleep.

30
03:01.431 --> 03:02.932
‎If you fail…

31
03:04.642 --> 03:06.185
‎you cost three people their lives.

32
03:07.478 --> 03:08.897
‎The one who donated this heart.

33
03:10.982 --> 03:12.358
‎The one here

34
03:13.359 --> 03:14.485
‎who is receiving this heart.

35
03:15.278 --> 03:16.321
‎And…

36
03:17.030 --> 03:19.073
‎the other person who could have

37
03:20.408 --> 03:21.409
‎received this heart.

38
03:29.751 --> 03:32.170
‎Yes. That's right.

39
03:36.216 --> 03:37.217
‎Aunt!

40
03:37.300 --> 03:38.301
‎Focus!

41
03:50.688 --> 03:51.689
‎Right now,

42
03:52.941 --> 03:54.567
‎you're all this patient has.

43
03:55.318 --> 03:56.402
‎You're everything to them.

44
03:58.780 --> 03:59.614
‎That's what it means

45
04:00.573 --> 04:01.574
‎to be a doctor.

46
04:10.708 --> 04:11.709
‎Focus.

47
04:12.961 --> 04:13.836
‎Yes, Doctor.

48
04:28.685 --> 04:31.813
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

49
04:32.397 --> 04:33.815
‎Let me repeat that.

50
04:33.898 --> 04:35.608
‎The vote must clear an 80%…

51
04:40.905 --> 04:41.948
‎An 80% majority.

52
04:42.448 --> 04:44.325
‎They probably haven't begun resection yet.

53
04:44.826 --> 04:46.869
‎Voting will now begin.

54
04:46.953 --> 04:48.496
‎We'll start with the front rows.

55
05:00.091 --> 05:01.259
‎Can you…

56
05:01.342 --> 05:03.136
‎No, I can't.

57
05:03.219 --> 05:05.847
‎This is the best I can do.

58
05:07.265 --> 05:09.934
‎Can't you go faster?

59
05:10.018 --> 05:11.477
‎I'll… I'll try.

60
05:13.980 --> 05:14.814
‎Metz.

61
05:15.815 --> 05:17.442
‎Tie off that spot, please.

62
05:18.067 --> 05:19.569
‎Oh, okay.

63
05:19.652 --> 05:21.279
‎-Hand me a tie. ‎-Yes, sir.

64
05:22.864 --> 05:24.324
‎I need to go faster…

65
05:24.407 --> 05:25.867
‎TIME: 01:41 P.M.

66
05:27.035 --> 05:28.494
‎They must be voting right now.

67
05:28.578 --> 05:30.580
‎POLLING BOOTH

68
05:34.000 --> 05:35.585
‎2:11 P.M. ‎SUNDAY, MAY 3

69
05:42.967 --> 05:46.637
‎Why aren't Director Bu ‎and Dr. Bae getting up?

70
05:47.221 --> 05:48.222
‎Man…

71
05:59.859 --> 06:00.902
‎WAITING ROOM

72
06:02.570 --> 06:03.571
‎Mi-gyeong.

73
06:03.654 --> 06:05.114
‎They're okay, right?

74
06:06.741 --> 06:09.660
‎They're in the middle of a long tunnel.

75
06:10.161 --> 06:12.455
‎They could really use some extra hands.

76
06:28.638 --> 06:29.472
‎Director Bu.

77
06:30.598 --> 06:31.599
‎Dr. Bae.

78
06:32.767 --> 06:34.310
‎Aren't you going to vote?

79
06:44.904 --> 06:46.239
‎Get up already!

80
07:07.844 --> 07:10.847
‎ARE YOU IN FAVOR OF INTERNS AND RESIDENTS ‎SUBMITTING THEIR RESIGNATIONS?

81
07:11.556 --> 07:12.932
‎Damn it.

82
07:15.518 --> 07:18.229
‎Director, you're going the wrong way!

83
07:25.111 --> 07:26.904
‎What's he doing?

84
07:28.739 --> 07:31.159
‎Right now,

85
07:31.826 --> 07:35.872
‎there's only one OR in our hospital ‎with a surgery underway.

86
07:37.039 --> 07:38.958
‎It's OR 7.

87
07:39.959 --> 07:42.003
‎Right now, the smallest child is lying

88
07:42.879 --> 07:45.131
‎in our largest operating room.

89
07:45.965 --> 07:46.883
‎That child

90
07:47.550 --> 07:49.510
‎was rejected repeatedly ‎by the main hospital,

91
07:49.594 --> 07:50.803
‎our own surgical team,

92
07:51.596 --> 07:54.515
‎and several other hospitals as well.

93
07:55.808 --> 07:57.268
‎But today,

94
07:57.351 --> 08:00.521
‎that child is receiving the surgery ‎no one else would do.

95
08:01.564 --> 08:02.482
‎The procedure involves

96
08:02.565 --> 08:05.401
‎taking six organs out of the body,

97
08:05.902 --> 08:07.487
‎resecting the tumor,

98
08:07.570 --> 08:09.739
‎and then putting them back in.

99
08:09.822 --> 08:15.036
‎It's called multivisceral ex vivo ‎tumor resection and autotransplantation.

100
08:17.163 --> 08:19.165
‎And it's an outrageous procedure.

101
08:21.584 --> 08:24.921
‎But this is that child's last resort.

102
08:27.423 --> 08:28.341
‎Ladies and gentlemen.

103
08:29.050 --> 08:30.593
‎If we are doctors…

104
08:30.676 --> 08:32.261
‎If we are real surgeons,

105
08:34.096 --> 08:36.599
‎where should we be right now?

106
08:40.228 --> 08:43.147
‎In this voting room, ‎putting our patients' lives on the line?

107
08:43.231 --> 08:44.148
‎Or…

108
08:45.691 --> 08:47.193
‎in that operating room?

109
08:53.908 --> 08:55.576
‎This is my decision.

110
09:02.750 --> 09:04.001
‎Has he lost his mind?

111
09:04.502 --> 09:06.170
‎What are you doing? Stop him!

112
09:12.093 --> 09:12.969
‎You know, right?

113
09:13.052 --> 09:16.389
‎Gye Su-jeong is doing ‎that multivisceral ex vivo procedure.

114
09:16.889 --> 09:19.433
‎But even she needs help with this.

115
09:19.517 --> 09:21.894
‎-Dr. Bae… ‎-Your niece is seven, right?

116
09:21.978 --> 09:22.853
‎This kid is eight.

117
09:22.937 --> 09:26.148
‎You'll feel guilty when you go home ‎and see your niece.

118
09:26.232 --> 09:27.984
‎Trust me on this, okay?

119
09:29.151 --> 09:30.069
‎Seong-gyu.

120
09:30.611 --> 09:31.737
‎Let's go help.

121
09:40.788 --> 09:42.331
‎Dr. Bae.

122
09:42.415 --> 09:43.874
‎Stop talking nonsense.

123
09:44.500 --> 09:46.669
‎Go and bring the director back.

124
09:46.752 --> 09:48.296
‎And you, hurry up and get on with it!

125
10:05.062 --> 10:07.857
‎All the votes are in.

126
10:09.567 --> 10:10.776
‎We'll begin counting…

127
10:15.489 --> 10:18.159
‎What the hell? Have they lost their minds?

128
10:19.368 --> 10:20.661
‎Where is OR 7?

129
10:24.498 --> 10:25.541
‎Come on…

130
10:30.296 --> 10:33.299
‎Dr. Do, pick up the pace. ‎We're tight on time.

131
10:33.382 --> 10:36.677
‎I'm doing my absolute best right now.

132
10:38.054 --> 10:40.306
‎I'm frustrated too!

133
10:40.389 --> 10:41.223
‎Focus, please.

134
10:41.974 --> 10:42.975
‎Yes, Doctor.

135
10:44.810 --> 10:46.062
‎Man…

136
10:46.145 --> 10:48.731
‎Can the three of us really pull this off?

137
10:48.814 --> 10:51.150
‎Save the questions and pick up the pace.

138
10:52.943 --> 10:55.279
‎Dr. Jo, please page someone.

139
10:55.863 --> 10:57.198
‎Disciplinary action or not,

140
10:57.698 --> 10:59.867
‎I can't believe no one came.

141
11:03.329 --> 11:05.373
‎Director Bu and Dr. Bae!

142
11:05.456 --> 11:07.333
‎We're going to make it!

143
11:07.416 --> 11:10.169
‎Hyeon-a, you're going to make it.

144
11:10.252 --> 11:11.295
‎I'm going to make it too!

145
11:11.379 --> 11:13.464
‎You've progressed ‎twice as fast as I expected.

146
11:13.547 --> 11:15.424
‎Should've been three times faster.

147
11:15.925 --> 11:17.843
‎You're really something…

148
11:17.927 --> 11:20.137
‎-Who are you? ‎-Grab the harmonic.

149
11:20.221 --> 11:22.098
‎Or cut with the Metz and tie off.

150
11:22.181 --> 11:23.140
‎Wait, you sound like…

151
11:23.849 --> 11:25.101
‎Ms. Jang?

152
11:25.851 --> 11:27.144
‎Director Jang Hui-suk?

153
11:27.228 --> 11:29.105
‎Please stop talking

154
11:29.188 --> 11:31.482
‎and get in here already!

155
11:32.983 --> 11:34.318
‎Thank you, Director.

156
11:34.402 --> 11:37.238
‎Thank you so much. ‎All of you are the best!

157
11:37.321 --> 11:39.573
‎But if you're here, Director…

158
11:40.074 --> 11:42.535
‎You voted before coming, right?

159
11:42.618 --> 11:43.536
‎Right?

160
11:49.625 --> 11:53.212
‎The overwhelming 92% approval rate

161
11:53.295 --> 11:55.881
‎reflects the deep anxiety and hardship

162
11:55.965 --> 11:59.009
‎young doctors have felt ‎in this profession.

163
12:00.010 --> 12:03.722
‎If the government ‎unjustly punishes us over this issue,

164
12:04.348 --> 12:09.019
‎we will stand united, ‎not as doctors, but as citizens.

165
12:09.103 --> 12:10.896
‎We became doctors

166
12:12.314 --> 12:13.899
‎to save patients in pain…

167
12:15.901 --> 12:18.154
‎Right now,

168
12:18.237 --> 12:21.157
‎there's only one OR in our hospital ‎with a surgery underway.

169
12:21.657 --> 12:23.784
‎It's OR 7.

170
12:24.368 --> 12:26.454
‎Right now, the smallest child is lying

171
12:27.288 --> 12:29.373
‎in our largest operating room.

172
12:32.460 --> 12:36.297
‎…to save patients in pain

173
12:37.214 --> 12:39.925
‎and to contribute ‎to Korea's medical advancement

174
12:40.718 --> 12:42.094
‎as well as

175
12:43.053 --> 12:44.054
‎its public health…

176
12:44.138 --> 12:46.015
‎Good job. I'll take it from here.

177
12:47.349 --> 12:48.350
‎Now then.

178
12:49.268 --> 12:52.021
‎The current administration ‎is pushing through

179
12:52.104 --> 12:54.940
‎this faulty policy without any dialogue,

180
12:56.108 --> 12:58.402
‎silencing its critics,

181
12:59.445 --> 13:02.281
‎and abusing its power to intimidate us.

182
13:02.364 --> 13:04.950
‎Is this what they call communication?

183
13:09.371 --> 13:12.875
‎But this is that child's last resort.

184
13:13.459 --> 13:14.585
‎If we are doctors…

185
13:15.461 --> 13:17.004
‎If we are real surgeons,

186
13:18.047 --> 13:20.424
‎where should we be right now?

187
13:20.925 --> 13:21.926
‎Seong-gyu.

188
13:22.635 --> 13:23.511
‎Let's go help.

189
13:24.720 --> 13:27.806
‎Let's show them we won't back down!

190
13:31.977 --> 13:33.395
‎EXPANDING QUOTA ‎RUINS EDUCATION

191
13:39.777 --> 13:41.362
‎Why am I so hot?

192
13:41.445 --> 13:43.405
‎It's really cold, but I'm burning up.

193
13:43.489 --> 13:45.449
‎-Should I wipe your forehead? ‎-Not yet.

194
13:46.325 --> 13:48.953
‎I think we're in the final stretch.

195
14:02.049 --> 14:04.051
‎Can you hear me, Director?

196
14:04.593 --> 14:06.762
‎Wait. Is that you, Dr. Do?

197
14:06.845 --> 14:08.430
‎I thought you went to the restroom.

198
14:08.514 --> 14:10.516
‎You've got a lot of nerve coming here.

199
14:11.100 --> 14:12.476
‎Come on, you know better.

200
14:12.560 --> 14:14.812
‎What are you doing here instead of voting?

201
14:15.437 --> 14:17.898
‎The IRB hasn't even approved this surgery.

202
14:17.982 --> 14:21.652
‎What am I looking at? Are those organs?

203
14:22.319 --> 14:23.654
‎Are you insane?

204
14:23.737 --> 14:27.324
‎This is a direct violation ‎of our hospital and foundation ethics!

205
14:27.825 --> 14:29.285
‎Stop the surgery!

206
14:29.368 --> 14:31.871
‎How is it ethical ‎to close someone up mid-surgery?

207
14:33.873 --> 14:35.791
‎I told you to stop the surgery!

208
14:37.585 --> 14:40.963
‎Ms. Lee Hyeon-a has never been to school.

209
14:41.714 --> 14:43.465
‎She's never given her mom any trouble.

210
14:44.216 --> 14:47.678
‎I hope Hyeon-a grows up ‎to be a huge troublemaker for her mom.

211
14:48.387 --> 14:50.598
‎I'm going to make sure

212
14:51.432 --> 14:53.517
‎Hyeon-a gets to grow up.

213
15:01.901 --> 15:03.611
‎We'll need to drag them out

214
15:03.694 --> 15:05.654
‎or bring in private security.

215
15:05.738 --> 15:06.822
‎Do it.

216
15:07.990 --> 15:09.325
‎Gu Bon-pyeong!

217
15:12.494 --> 15:13.662
‎On my authority as director,

218
15:14.246 --> 15:17.082
‎we're seeing this surgery ‎through to the end.

219
15:28.302 --> 15:30.012
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon!

220
15:30.095 --> 15:33.349
‎You just made a terrible mistake… ‎No, a terrible choice!

221
15:33.432 --> 15:36.560
‎You call the chairman of the foundation ‎and Magnolia by his name?

222
15:36.644 --> 15:38.520
‎-Dr. Jo, do what you do best. ‎-That damn title

223
15:38.604 --> 15:41.565
‎must've gone to your head!

224
15:41.649 --> 15:43.150
‎How dare you…

225
15:43.233 --> 15:45.152
‎What's the matter with you?

226
15:58.165 --> 15:59.875
‎What the hell?

227
15:59.959 --> 16:01.460
‎-They turned off the mic? ‎-Let's go.

228
16:01.543 --> 16:03.253
‎-Are you serious? ‎-Damn it.

229
16:24.483 --> 16:26.235
‎I'll call in private security.

230
16:26.735 --> 16:29.113
‎Hey, call management.

231
16:29.822 --> 16:31.073
‎There's a CCTV camera in there.

232
16:31.156 --> 16:31.991
‎What?

233
16:33.117 --> 16:34.284
‎So what?

234
16:34.368 --> 16:35.744
‎It's pediatric surgery.

235
16:36.578 --> 16:39.456
‎If anyone goes in to stop it ‎or contaminates the OR,

236
16:39.540 --> 16:41.667
‎and the footage gets leaked to the public,

237
16:42.751 --> 16:44.628
‎it won't be good for the strike.

238
16:44.712 --> 16:46.505
‎Those damn CCTV cameras…

239
16:46.588 --> 16:48.841
‎We need a valid reason ‎to take them down for good.

240
16:49.842 --> 16:52.094
‎And I'm going to make sure they stay down.

241
16:52.177 --> 16:53.137
‎Call a meeting.

242
16:53.220 --> 16:54.096
‎Yes, sir.

243
17:00.269 --> 17:02.521
‎Beginning reconstruction.

244
17:09.528 --> 17:10.446
‎Dr. Kim.

245
17:10.529 --> 17:12.197
‎Sorry to keep you all waiting.

246
17:12.281 --> 17:13.574
‎-Damn it. ‎-Hey, everyone.

247
17:13.657 --> 17:17.202
‎I'm finally… I'm here…

248
17:21.457 --> 17:23.333
‎What can I do, Dr. Jo?

249
17:23.417 --> 17:25.627
‎I knew you'd show up, ‎so I texted you not to.

250
17:26.211 --> 17:27.671
‎Even the director is here.

251
17:28.380 --> 17:30.007
‎But who is that over there?

252
17:30.841 --> 17:32.634
‎Stop whispering and start moving.

253
17:32.718 --> 17:35.679
‎-The organs are going back in. ‎-Okay, got it.

254
17:40.225 --> 17:42.561
‎IVC reconstructed with a synthetic graft.

255
17:43.812 --> 17:44.897
‎Now we re-implant the organs.

256
17:45.439 --> 17:46.273
‎Yes, Doctor.

257
18:33.737 --> 18:35.364
‎OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

258
18:36.949 --> 18:38.742
‎Clamps coming off.

259
18:39.409 --> 18:41.286
‎-Is the saline ready? ‎-Yes.

260
18:41.870 --> 18:42.955
‎Coming off now.

261
18:57.344 --> 18:59.972
‎Keep going. This is important.

262
19:00.055 --> 19:01.890
‎-Yes, Doctor. ‎-No signs of bleeding.

263
19:01.974 --> 19:03.684
‎The sutures are holding.

264
19:03.767 --> 19:07.104
‎This part always puts me on edge.

265
19:07.187 --> 19:08.188
‎Right?

266
19:08.272 --> 19:10.899
‎If the organs don't pink up, ‎it means they're damaged.

267
19:10.983 --> 19:14.194
‎Which means all the work we've done,

268
19:14.278 --> 19:15.821
‎plus Hyeon-a's organs…

269
19:15.904 --> 19:17.406
‎Will just go to waste.

270
19:22.494 --> 19:25.622
‎Why… why isn't the color returning?

271
19:27.958 --> 19:30.127
‎Am I the only one not seeing it?

272
19:30.210 --> 19:32.462
‎Prep more saline. Make it warmer.

273
19:33.046 --> 19:33.881
‎Yes, sir.

274
19:34.423 --> 19:36.258
‎Come on, Hyeon-a!

275
19:36.341 --> 19:38.302
‎-Check for clots on the ultrasound? ‎-Yes.

276
19:38.385 --> 19:41.847
‎Hey, it's back! The color's returning!

277
19:52.733 --> 19:53.567
‎BP?

278
19:55.736 --> 19:56.737
‎It hasn't dropped.

279
19:57.321 --> 19:58.363
‎Let's turn off the shunt.

280
19:58.447 --> 20:00.115
‎I'll do it!

281
20:39.655 --> 20:40.864
‎She looks so…

282
20:42.574 --> 20:43.575
‎Small.

283
20:44.826 --> 20:45.827
‎She's so…

284
20:46.703 --> 20:47.871
‎Very small.

285
20:49.748 --> 20:50.832
‎Hyeon-a.

286
20:52.000 --> 20:53.961
‎Hyeon-a…

287
20:54.044 --> 20:55.796
‎You did a great job.

288
21:03.470 --> 21:04.304
‎Dr. Gye.

289
21:06.974 --> 21:08.058
‎Surgery is complete.

290
21:11.103 --> 21:12.271
‎A great job hanging in there…

291
21:26.159 --> 21:27.286
‎Nicely done.

292
21:30.289 --> 21:31.164
‎Everyone…

293
21:33.125 --> 21:36.169
‎-Thank you-- ‎-Please don't bow!

294
21:36.962 --> 21:40.132
‎We all ended up here because you bowed.

295
21:41.133 --> 21:43.343
‎Stop acting out of character.

296
21:43.427 --> 21:46.138
‎Just do what you usually do and leave.

297
22:57.042 --> 22:58.376
‎How did it go?

298
23:23.860 --> 23:24.694
‎Thank you.

299
23:25.529 --> 23:26.696
‎Thank you.

300
23:30.408 --> 23:32.494
‎-Thank you, Dr. Gye! ‎-Thank you, Dr. Gye!

301
23:44.422 --> 23:45.590
‎Good job.

302
23:52.389 --> 23:54.391
‎Not handling it well, is she?

303
23:55.767 --> 23:56.893
‎It's no wonder.

304
23:56.977 --> 23:59.146
‎She didn't do it to get thanks.

305
24:01.022 --> 24:03.942
‎Right. That's our Su-jeong.

306
24:16.663 --> 24:19.166
‎Man, what the heck?

307
24:19.249 --> 24:21.501
‎I got a leg cramp.

308
24:22.961 --> 24:24.212
‎Dr. Kim.

309
24:25.422 --> 24:29.384
‎You just betrayed ‎everything we stand for as doctors.

310
24:30.760 --> 24:31.928
‎It's just a habit.

311
24:32.012 --> 24:33.388
‎We all experienced the miracle

312
24:33.471 --> 24:36.975
‎of our grandmothers ‎using folk remedies to…

313
24:37.058 --> 24:39.644
‎Wait a minute. I got another cramp.

314
24:40.270 --> 24:42.939
‎Give me a break. You showed up at the end.

315
24:43.023 --> 24:44.691
‎It's been a while since I operated.

316
24:44.774 --> 24:47.444
‎If we put it that way, ‎the same goes for you, Dr. Bae.

317
24:48.820 --> 24:51.239
‎You weren't there from the start either.

318
24:58.705 --> 24:59.539
‎I knew it.

319
24:59.623 --> 25:01.958
‎Ms. Jang and I are on the same wavelength.

320
25:02.042 --> 25:03.126
‎Let's go, everyone.

321
25:03.210 --> 25:04.461
‎What? Go where?

322
25:04.544 --> 25:05.629
‎Work dinner, of course.

323
25:06.213 --> 25:07.214
‎Work dinner?

324
25:07.297 --> 25:09.966
‎Dr. Gye and Ms. Jang are buying dinner

325
25:10.050 --> 25:11.593
‎because we worked so hard.

326
25:12.552 --> 25:14.095
‎-Really? ‎-Let's go!

327
25:14.179 --> 25:16.097
‎-That was unexpected. ‎-Yeah. Let's go.

328
25:17.557 --> 25:19.601
‎Here, take this.

329
25:20.143 --> 25:22.187
‎-Eung-gu, we need pickled radish here too. ‎-Got it.

330
25:22.687 --> 25:24.356
‎-Here you go. ‎-Thanks.

331
25:26.608 --> 25:28.360
‎-Here you go. ‎-Thank you.

332
25:31.947 --> 25:32.822
‎Attention, everyone.

333
25:33.573 --> 25:34.741
‎With the strike going on,

334
25:34.824 --> 25:37.452
‎everything around the hospital ‎closed early.

335
25:37.535 --> 25:40.080
‎This was the closest place open this late.

336
25:40.163 --> 25:41.998
‎I saw open Korean BBQ places ‎on the way here.

337
25:42.082 --> 25:43.333
‎I saw at least two.

338
25:44.834 --> 25:46.795
‎Right, that's why

339
25:46.878 --> 25:49.047
‎I ordered all 25 items on the menu.

340
25:49.965 --> 25:52.717
‎So don't hold back and enjoy the food.

341
25:53.343 --> 25:56.638
‎Thank you so much for today, everyone.

342
25:56.721 --> 25:59.015
‎-Good job. ‎-Good job, everyone.

343
26:01.059 --> 26:03.895
‎And don't forget to take ‎my business card afterward.

344
26:04.562 --> 26:06.731
‎All right. Cheers!

345
26:06.815 --> 26:09.192
‎-Cheers! ‎-Great job, everyone.

346
26:09.276 --> 26:10.986
‎-Good job. ‎-Good job.

347
26:11.069 --> 26:13.113
‎-Nice work. ‎-Nice work.

348
26:13.196 --> 26:15.573
‎Great job, everyone.

349
26:15.657 --> 26:16.491
‎You too.

350
26:17.492 --> 26:18.910
‎Excuse me, everyone.

351
26:18.994 --> 26:20.704
‎As a doctor,

352
26:21.288 --> 26:22.122
‎I…

353
26:22.998 --> 26:24.374
‎I was really moved--

354
26:24.457 --> 26:25.500
‎Let's eat.

355
26:25.583 --> 26:27.252
‎-Let's eat. ‎-Let's eat.

356
26:27.335 --> 26:29.129
‎Let's eat.

357
26:29.629 --> 26:31.339
‎Take your time eating.

358
26:31.423 --> 26:32.841
‎No one's taking your food away.

359
26:37.721 --> 26:39.639
‎This place is open 24 hours, right?

360
26:40.390 --> 26:43.351
‎Yes. Are you asking ‎so you can eat for 24 hours straight?

361
26:43.435 --> 26:45.812
‎Sleep, wake up, eat, and repeat?

362
26:46.396 --> 26:48.606
‎That's a question only you'd ask, Dr. Gye.

363
26:53.737 --> 26:56.031
‎They say there's no paradise to escape to,

364
26:56.114 --> 26:57.115
‎but look at the name here.

365
26:57.699 --> 26:58.658
‎It's "Gimbap Paradise."

366
26:58.742 --> 26:59.576
‎GIMBAP PARADISE

367
26:59.659 --> 27:01.244
‎This is Su-jeong's paradise.

368
27:03.371 --> 27:04.873
‎This is good. It's all good.

369
27:12.714 --> 27:13.882
‎Yes, it's good.

370
27:13.965 --> 27:16.051
‎Director, do you eat snack bar food?

371
27:16.134 --> 27:17.344
‎It's been a while, but it's good.

372
27:18.219 --> 27:19.971
‎-Everyone, please eat. ‎-Right.

373
27:22.807 --> 27:26.436
‎It's been a while ‎since we shared a meal like this

374
27:26.519 --> 27:27.729
‎after surviving the trenches.

375
27:27.812 --> 27:29.356
‎So let's eat.

376
27:29.439 --> 27:30.648
‎Yes, sir. Let's eat!

377
27:33.777 --> 27:35.153
‎Thank you, Dr. Do.

378
27:39.115 --> 27:39.949
‎Dr. Gye.

379
27:42.118 --> 27:44.287
‎You did very good work today.

380
27:54.964 --> 27:55.799
‎Thank you, sir.

381
27:57.509 --> 27:59.427
‎Look at you, being all nice and social.

382
28:02.305 --> 28:03.515
‎Excuse me, everyone.

383
28:05.767 --> 28:08.353
‎When you came today, I felt so…

384
28:08.937 --> 28:10.146
‎I felt so…

385
28:11.022 --> 28:13.024
‎I was just so…

386
28:13.108 --> 28:15.443
‎Seriously, thank you so much.

387
28:15.527 --> 28:17.153
‎Did that yogurt make you drunk?

388
28:17.237 --> 28:20.240
‎Seriously? Work dinner at a snack bar?

389
28:20.323 --> 28:23.118
‎In that case, I'm having ‎rabokki‎ first.

390
28:27.163 --> 28:30.291
‎Everything tastes good ‎after a hard day's work, right?

391
28:30.375 --> 28:32.585
‎Put it down. I've had my eye on that.

392
28:32.669 --> 28:34.254
‎Have the ‎jjolbokki‎. It's the same thing.

393
28:34.337 --> 28:36.673
‎-Dr. Gye wanted it too. ‎-Hey!

394
28:36.756 --> 28:37.841
‎Director Bu wants some.

395
28:37.924 --> 28:40.385
‎-No, this is for Dr. Gye. ‎-I can't trick you.

396
28:40.969 --> 28:42.178
‎I'm having the pork cutlet.

397
28:42.262 --> 28:44.556
‎Dr. Bae, can you pass the dumplings?

398
28:45.056 --> 28:46.266
‎-This? ‎-Yes.

399
28:46.349 --> 28:47.559
‎-Here. ‎-Thank you.

400
28:47.642 --> 28:49.602
‎-This is good. ‎-It's delicious.

401
28:49.686 --> 28:51.354
‎Drink some water too.

402
28:51.438 --> 28:52.439
‎You'll get indigestion.

403
28:52.939 --> 28:54.816
‎This sauce is really good.

404
28:55.900 --> 28:57.444
‎-Don't rush. ‎-Any beer?

405
28:57.527 --> 28:58.611
‎Are you going to cry?

406
28:59.404 --> 29:00.488
‎What do you mean?

407
29:01.072 --> 29:03.408
‎Is it because Su-jeong made friends?

408
29:05.744 --> 29:07.120
‎Friends? They're just colleagues.

409
29:07.912 --> 29:10.248
‎Su-jeong doesn't look lonely, does she?

410
29:13.501 --> 29:15.170
‎-Drink some water. ‎-It's nice.

411
29:15.712 --> 29:17.505
‎-Can I have the pork cutlet? ‎-Go ahead.

412
29:17.589 --> 29:19.883
‎I'm seriously good at it.

413
29:19.966 --> 29:21.509
‎-Really? ‎-Yeah.

414
29:21.593 --> 29:23.470
‎-Want to see? ‎-Right now?

415
29:23.553 --> 29:24.846
‎-Oh, come on. ‎-Watch me.

416
29:24.929 --> 29:27.348
‎-Are you ready? ‎-Just watch.

417
29:37.776 --> 29:38.985
‎You're good!

418
29:39.068 --> 29:39.986
‎Can I try it too?

419
29:40.904 --> 29:42.614
‎-Of course! ‎-Really?

420
29:42.697 --> 29:44.240
‎Can you catch a dumpling?

421
29:44.324 --> 29:46.159
‎-Dumpling? Definitely. ‎-Are you sure?

422
29:46.242 --> 29:48.620
‎-I can do a dumpling. ‎-I'll toss one then.

423
29:49.329 --> 29:50.705
‎One, two, three.

424
29:56.169 --> 29:57.879
‎I'll set her down here.

425
29:57.962 --> 29:59.088
‎Goodness.

426
29:59.172 --> 30:00.131
‎Here we go.

427
30:00.215 --> 30:01.674
‎-She's totally out. ‎-Goodness.

428
30:01.758 --> 30:03.843
‎-Oh dear. ‎-Are you okay?

429
30:03.927 --> 30:05.512
‎I'm okay. Gosh, my back hurts.

430
30:05.595 --> 30:07.430
‎When did she get so heavy?

431
30:08.264 --> 30:09.182
‎Eung-gu.

432
30:09.724 --> 30:12.018
‎You get to carry her onto the bus.

433
30:17.440 --> 30:21.194
‎I knitted so much at the hospital earlier

434
30:21.277 --> 30:22.403
‎that my eyes are killing me.

435
30:23.029 --> 30:25.532
‎-My back is killing me too. ‎-Seriously?

436
30:25.615 --> 30:28.201
‎-I'll carry her. ‎-No, it's fine.

437
30:28.284 --> 30:30.954
‎Between planning the surgery ‎and stressing over it,

438
30:31.538 --> 30:34.207
‎she probably hasn't slept in days.

439
30:35.250 --> 30:38.962
‎Thank you for taking care of Su-jeong.

440
30:39.045 --> 30:41.881
‎Not at all. I'm the one ‎who should be thankful.

441
30:42.382 --> 30:44.300
‎-Oh, this is good. ‎-What?

442
30:44.384 --> 30:46.261
‎Your bus arrives before ours, Dr. Park.

443
30:47.720 --> 30:49.597
‎I'll go after I see you off.

444
30:49.681 --> 30:52.642
‎No, it's okay. There are four of us here.

445
30:52.725 --> 30:54.227
‎But you're alone.

446
30:54.936 --> 30:56.646
‎We can't just leave you here.

447
30:57.272 --> 30:59.440
‎It's lonely waiting for the bus alone.

448
31:04.612 --> 31:07.240
‎By the way, Ms. Jang…

449
31:07.323 --> 31:10.743
‎How did you end up ‎teaching and caring for your niece?

450
31:16.040 --> 31:17.000
‎Well, actually…

451
31:18.084 --> 31:19.794
‎We're not related by blood.

452
31:19.878 --> 31:22.213
‎What? Really?

453
31:23.923 --> 31:25.884
‎Then how…

454
31:28.678 --> 31:31.639
‎She's the daughter of my closest friend.

455
31:32.765 --> 31:33.933
‎After she passed away,

456
31:34.017 --> 31:35.476
‎it just kind of happened.

457
31:37.812 --> 31:39.606
‎She was my savior, you know.

458
31:41.190 --> 31:42.901
‎She took me in as family.

459
31:46.446 --> 31:49.407
‎Su-jeong is the only family I have.

460
31:50.867 --> 31:51.826
‎I mean, we have.

461
31:57.957 --> 31:59.834
‎Your family reminds me of my own.

462
32:01.711 --> 32:02.670
‎-What? ‎-What?

463
32:05.632 --> 32:06.591
‎Then are you…

464
32:08.885 --> 32:12.597
‎My parents used to ‎volunteer at a children's home.

465
32:13.181 --> 32:15.600
‎They said I was ‎always sitting in the corner,

466
32:15.683 --> 32:17.393
‎showing no emotion at all.

467
32:18.561 --> 32:21.856
‎They were so heartbroken ‎that they would cry at home all the time.

468
32:22.440 --> 32:25.151
‎But I don't remember any of that.

469
32:25.234 --> 32:26.736
‎I just wonder if I really did that.

470
32:28.905 --> 32:30.698
‎Anyway, they said

471
32:30.782 --> 32:33.534
‎all they wanted was to take me in ‎and make me smile.

472
32:34.577 --> 32:37.455
‎Of course. ‎They wanted to give you a warm bed,

473
32:38.498 --> 32:40.166
‎dress you in warm clothes,

474
32:41.459 --> 32:43.378
‎and feed you warm meals.

475
32:44.587 --> 32:45.546
‎Right.

476
32:45.630 --> 32:47.173
‎I guess all parents think alike.

477
32:51.761 --> 32:53.429
‎Having a family

478
32:54.722 --> 32:55.890
‎is really wonderful.

479
32:59.018 --> 33:01.270
‎I realized the same ‎after finding myself with one.

480
33:02.355 --> 33:03.272
‎It's wonderful.

481
33:07.610 --> 33:10.822
‎Dr. Park, thank you so much for today.

482
33:10.905 --> 33:12.365
‎No, not at all.

483
33:13.574 --> 33:14.492
‎You know…

484
33:16.202 --> 33:20.081
‎I don't think I'll ever forget today.

485
33:21.582 --> 33:22.709
‎This was…

486
33:24.377 --> 33:26.754
‎the closest I've felt to being a doctor.

487
33:30.383 --> 33:32.802
‎-Bus 320 will be arriving shortly. ‎-Oh.

488
33:33.386 --> 33:34.762
‎I'll get going now.

489
33:34.846 --> 33:36.347
‎Goodbye, young doctor.

490
33:36.431 --> 33:37.515
‎Goodbye, sir.

491
33:37.598 --> 33:39.517
‎-Get home safely. ‎-I will.

492
33:41.144 --> 33:42.770
‎He's leaving. No, this way.

493
33:42.854 --> 33:43.938
‎He's over there.

494
34:05.835 --> 34:07.086
‎Where's my phone?

495
34:09.714 --> 34:11.549
‎DAD ‎MOM

496
34:11.632 --> 34:13.468
‎MOM: ARE YOU STILL AT THE HOSPITAL?

497
34:13.551 --> 34:15.678
‎Son, I know you must be busy.

498
34:15.762 --> 34:17.722
‎Still, I'm getting worried ‎because I can't reach you.

499
34:17.805 --> 34:19.807
‎Are you eating okay?

500
34:19.891 --> 34:21.142
‎I miss hearing your voice.

501
34:25.271 --> 34:26.355
‎DAD

502
34:26.439 --> 34:28.900
‎Your mom is worried ‎because you're not picking up.

503
34:28.983 --> 34:32.278
‎I told her to stop calling you ‎because studying to be a doctor is hard.

504
34:32.361 --> 34:34.155
‎You're not sick, are you?

505
34:35.448 --> 34:36.991
‎I'm not sick.

506
34:37.075 --> 34:38.451
‎I'll call Mom later.

507
34:54.801 --> 34:58.679
‎ONYU NURSING HOME

508
35:11.734 --> 35:13.236
‎It's just us for round two!

509
35:13.319 --> 35:14.737
‎Sounds great.

510
35:18.449 --> 35:19.492
‎Here we go.

511
35:20.493 --> 35:22.036
‎-Cheers! ‎-Cheers!

512
35:32.296 --> 35:33.256
‎Today's surgery

513
35:34.257 --> 35:36.217
‎was probably the director's last.

514
35:37.343 --> 35:39.512
‎He's losing his central vision.

515
35:40.388 --> 35:42.181
‎Oh dear…

516
35:50.940 --> 35:52.817
‎Hold on. Are you crying?

517
35:52.900 --> 35:55.653
‎No. It's not a full-on sob session.

518
35:57.780 --> 35:58.739
‎It's just…

519
36:00.950 --> 36:03.995
‎What I did today feels like a dream.

520
36:05.538 --> 36:07.707
‎I'm a doctor by profession,

521
36:07.790 --> 36:10.209
‎but I don't think ‎I've ever lived as a real doctor.

522
36:18.009 --> 36:18.843
‎But today,

523
36:19.844 --> 36:22.847
‎I saved a person.

524
36:34.734 --> 36:36.819
‎I saved the life of a child.

525
36:39.947 --> 36:42.074
‎You save lives every single day.

526
36:42.909 --> 36:43.784
‎All of us do.

527
36:44.702 --> 36:45.578
‎Right.

528
36:47.163 --> 36:48.331
‎You're right.

529
36:48.414 --> 36:49.332
‎I guess…

530
36:50.583 --> 36:52.877
‎it's been a long time ‎since I've thought about that.

531
36:54.629 --> 36:56.839
‎The burden of holding

532
36:57.632 --> 37:00.343
‎a human life in my hands.

533
37:01.219 --> 37:04.639
‎Or maybe I've just been avoiding it…

534
37:06.224 --> 37:07.642
‎since I'm incompetent.

535
37:09.101 --> 37:11.979
‎Come on. You only had one sip of beer!

536
37:24.283 --> 37:25.493
‎Today…

537
37:26.452 --> 37:27.495
‎I was a doctor.

538
37:29.205 --> 37:30.414
‎Yes, you were.

539
37:37.588 --> 37:39.882
‎What? Is it funny seeing me cry?

540
37:39.966 --> 37:41.676
‎No, it's not that.

541
37:41.759 --> 37:43.511
‎The way the director yelled,

542
37:44.553 --> 37:46.764
‎"Gu Bon-pyeong!"

543
37:49.809 --> 37:52.311
‎It was so satisfying!

544
37:54.313 --> 37:55.815
‎Did you see Kim Chang-su's face?

545
37:55.898 --> 37:58.192
‎I hate that jerk even more.

546
37:59.610 --> 38:01.028
‎I forgot tomorrow was coming.

547
38:03.823 --> 38:05.283
‎Is it starting to hit you now?

548
38:05.366 --> 38:06.409
‎Yeah.

549
38:06.492 --> 38:08.536
‎I think Director Bu lost his mind.

550
38:09.120 --> 38:12.206
‎-And I'm about to lose it myself. ‎-Same here.

551
38:14.750 --> 38:16.752
‎We all lost our minds today.

552
38:19.088 --> 38:20.923
‎Still,

553
38:21.007 --> 38:23.092
‎tomorrow is a whole new day.

554
38:24.093 --> 38:26.804
‎And after today, days like yesterday

555
38:26.887 --> 38:29.015
‎are over for good.

556
38:31.267 --> 38:34.478
‎Damn it, I'm still screwed.

557
38:35.604 --> 38:36.939
‎Man…

558
38:44.530 --> 38:47.366
‎I LOVE YOU, UNCLE

559
39:05.259 --> 39:06.135
‎You've grown.

560
39:07.720 --> 39:09.305
‎But you're still less than six spans tall.

561
39:10.514 --> 39:11.807
‎Why are you so small?

562
39:14.560 --> 39:15.728
‎Your niece is seven, right?

563
39:15.811 --> 39:17.229
‎This kid is eight.

564
39:17.313 --> 39:18.981
‎You'll feel guilty when you go home

565
39:19.523 --> 39:20.816
‎and see your niece.

566
39:20.900 --> 39:23.069
‎Trust me on this, okay?

567
39:23.152 --> 39:24.737
‎Seong-gyu. Let's go help.

568
39:27.615 --> 39:28.699
‎Damn it.

569
39:31.410 --> 39:32.453
‎He was right.

570
39:43.172 --> 39:44.882
‎Dr. Bae, how was the surgery‎…

571
39:44.965 --> 39:45.800
‎DR. BAE HEUNG-GON

572
39:50.721 --> 39:52.473
‎Dr. Bae, I'm sorry about earlier…

573
39:55.726 --> 39:57.937
‎Dr. Bae, how is the child…

574
40:03.025 --> 40:04.402
‎Surgery went well.

575
40:04.944 --> 40:06.821
‎The child has a chance now.

576
40:08.155 --> 40:09.198
‎Seong-gyu.

577
40:10.116 --> 40:11.450
‎Take care of yourself.

578
40:35.057 --> 40:36.725
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

579
40:36.809 --> 40:38.686
‎Something's off.

580
40:39.854 --> 40:41.730
‎Why is it so quiet?

581
40:42.731 --> 40:45.151
‎So I'm not the only one ‎who feels this way.

582
40:45.234 --> 40:46.902
‎You don't startle me anymore.

583
40:46.986 --> 40:48.362
‎I knew you'd come, Buzzkill Won-jin.

584
40:48.446 --> 40:49.697
‎It's weird, right?

585
40:49.780 --> 40:51.824
‎There's no one in front of the hospital.

586
40:52.575 --> 40:54.034
‎No reporters,

587
40:54.118 --> 40:56.829
‎no patients, and no doctors.

588
40:57.663 --> 40:59.290
‎There are days like this.

589
40:59.373 --> 41:01.375
‎Maybe it's because yesterday was hectic.

590
41:01.459 --> 41:03.335
‎It feels unusually peaceful today.

591
41:16.974 --> 41:17.808
‎What?

592
41:18.684 --> 41:19.768
‎Huh?

593
41:19.852 --> 41:21.520
‎PERSONNEL CHANGES

594
41:21.604 --> 41:22.605
‎SUSPENSION FROM DUTIES

595
41:22.688 --> 41:26.775
‎BU SEUNG-GWON, DO YUN-SIK, BAE HEUNG-GON, ‎JO WON-JIN, KIM SEONG-JIN, PARK TAE-GYEONG

596
41:30.029 --> 41:32.239
‎CONTRACT TERMINATION ‎GENERAL SURGERY, GYE SU-JEONG

597
41:34.533 --> 41:35.534
‎Damn it.

598
41:43.417 --> 41:45.961
‎So, after ignoring our repeated requests,

599
41:46.045 --> 41:48.714
‎the IRB suddenly decided to convene

600
41:48.797 --> 41:50.633
‎and review yesterday's procedure?

601
41:50.716 --> 41:53.844
‎And we're all suspended ‎from duties until then?

602
41:54.845 --> 41:58.015
‎Emergency or not, ‎if you perform an unapproved procedure,

603
41:58.098 --> 42:00.768
‎you're still subject to a post hoc review.

604
42:00.851 --> 42:02.478
‎You know that.

605
42:03.395 --> 42:07.149
‎But a post hoc review doesn't ‎automatically suspend you from duties.

606
42:07.233 --> 42:10.027
‎This is just a disciplinary hearing.

607
42:10.110 --> 42:11.320
‎So why…

608
42:12.613 --> 42:14.073
‎Why did you do that yesterday?

609
42:14.740 --> 42:16.951
‎What got into you, Director?

610
42:17.034 --> 42:18.077
‎If I'm suspended from duties…

611
42:19.537 --> 42:21.997
‎I have to leave this office, right?

612
42:25.167 --> 42:28.337
‎The meeting is taking place this evening.

613
42:28.420 --> 42:32.591
‎You should talk to the chairman ‎and Magnolia members beforehand--

614
42:32.675 --> 42:34.093
‎I know who the internal members are.

615
42:34.176 --> 42:36.887
‎But there are external ‎multidisciplinary members too.

616
42:36.971 --> 42:37.805
‎Who are they?

617
42:39.765 --> 42:41.475
‎The external medical expert is

618
42:42.142 --> 42:44.395
‎President Kim Chang-su ‎of the Medical Association.

619
42:44.478 --> 42:47.106
‎And the patient representative ‎is Chairman Park Gwang-cheol.

620
42:48.482 --> 42:52.570
‎Aren't people with direct conflicts ‎of interest supposed to be excluded?

621
42:53.612 --> 42:55.698
‎The legal expert is Attorney Won Ju-pil.

622
42:56.365 --> 42:57.199
‎I see.

623
42:57.950 --> 42:58.993
‎Do you know him?

624
43:01.620 --> 43:02.705
‎He's the attorney for Magnolia.

625
43:03.455 --> 43:04.665
‎Oh…

626
43:13.132 --> 43:14.425
‎Let's eat.

627
43:20.139 --> 43:22.182
‎Am I a glutton for enjoying pizza

628
43:22.683 --> 43:23.517
‎at a time like this?

629
43:23.601 --> 43:24.727
‎No, that'd be her.

630
43:24.810 --> 43:26.270
‎Hey, excuse me.

631
43:26.353 --> 43:29.690
‎How about a reaction? ‎Give me some credit for treating you guys.

632
43:33.319 --> 43:36.155
‎"There's a burst of basil in every bite!"

633
43:36.238 --> 43:38.407
‎"You can never go wrong with pizza."

634
43:38.490 --> 43:39.950
‎"Dr. Kim, you're the best!"

635
43:40.034 --> 43:41.744
‎Like this, Dr. Gye.

636
43:43.412 --> 43:44.955
‎Dr. Kim, you're the best!

637
43:49.335 --> 43:52.713
‎I texted you not to come to the OR ‎because we had enough doctors.

638
43:52.796 --> 43:54.632
‎Why did you insist on coming?

639
43:54.715 --> 43:57.134
‎You barely did anything, ‎and now you're facing discipline.

640
43:57.760 --> 44:01.096
‎Why do you always march ‎to the beat of your own drum?

641
44:01.180 --> 44:02.264
‎Gosh, this tastes good.

642
44:03.390 --> 44:04.808
‎How did you know?

643
44:04.892 --> 44:07.811
‎I played the drum in the ‎samulnori ‎club ‎before I joined the theater club.

644
44:07.895 --> 44:10.898
‎Call me if you need someone ‎to put on a show.

645
44:10.981 --> 44:13.025
‎And what do you mean ‎I barely did anything?

646
44:13.817 --> 44:15.444
‎I did all sorts of things.

647
44:16.028 --> 44:18.322
‎We begged them to approve the procedure,

648
44:18.405 --> 44:19.907
‎but they refused due to the strike.

649
44:21.200 --> 44:24.536
‎Still, we submitted everything ‎we had put together,

650
44:24.620 --> 44:25.663
‎so it'll be okay, right?

651
44:26.372 --> 44:27.706
‎I doubt it.

652
44:28.457 --> 44:29.708
‎Did you tell Ms. Jang?

653
44:31.043 --> 44:33.379
‎-Yes. ‎-I bet she got really mad.

654
44:34.630 --> 44:36.215
‎"I got fired. The IRB is convening."

655
44:38.759 --> 44:41.053
‎"Okay. See you later."

656
44:41.136 --> 44:42.513
‎"We'll wait and see."

657
44:43.931 --> 44:45.307
‎That's even scarier.

658
44:47.351 --> 44:48.268
‎Since I got fired,

659
44:49.603 --> 44:51.230
‎I can clock out, right?

660
44:51.313 --> 44:54.400
‎Instead of beating a drum, ‎can you beat some sense into her?

661
44:55.150 --> 44:57.653
‎Yesterday was my first time ‎seeing Dr. Gye operate.

662
44:57.736 --> 44:59.279
‎She was so impressive

663
44:59.363 --> 45:01.615
‎that I didn't recognize her ‎and almost introduced myself.

664
45:01.698 --> 45:04.034
‎I guess that side of her ‎is still in the OR.

665
45:04.701 --> 45:06.161
‎What are we going to do?

666
45:07.955 --> 45:10.457
‎We were all trying to save a patient.

667
45:10.541 --> 45:13.210
‎We'll need to take responsibility ‎as doctors and as adults.

668
45:14.169 --> 45:16.130
‎I'm ready to face any outcome.

669
45:16.630 --> 45:18.715
‎I'm fine as long as Hyeon-a's okay.

670
45:19.675 --> 45:22.136
‎The patient might sue ‎depending on the IRB's decision.

671
45:23.178 --> 45:24.138
‎Really?

672
45:24.638 --> 45:27.141
‎Do you really think ‎Hyeon-a's mother will sue us?

673
45:27.808 --> 45:30.018
‎Even though Hyeon-a stands a chance now?

674
45:30.102 --> 45:31.854
‎Dr. Jo, what made you this way?

675
45:31.937 --> 45:33.564
‎You have zero faith in patients.

676
45:34.690 --> 45:37.860
‎I bet that's why ‎the hospital is empty right now.

677
45:38.485 --> 45:39.987
‎Lack of faith ‎between patients and doctors.

678
45:44.324 --> 45:45.159
‎Hello?

679
45:45.742 --> 45:46.994
‎I'm outside on hospital grounds.

680
45:48.662 --> 45:49.705
‎Take them in.

681
45:49.788 --> 45:52.082
‎No, take them. I'll be right there.

682
45:52.166 --> 45:53.292
‎See you.

683
45:53.375 --> 45:55.210
‎You're suspended from duties. ‎You can't take patients.

684
45:55.294 --> 45:58.589
‎A big fire broke out at the building ‎near the park intersection.

685
45:58.672 --> 46:01.425
‎You know the firefighter ‎who always comes to the ER?

686
46:01.508 --> 46:03.177
‎-They're bringing him in. ‎-Dr. Kim!

687
46:03.260 --> 46:05.429
‎You'll face even more disciplinary action!

688
46:05.512 --> 46:07.306
‎I don't care if I'm suspended. ‎I need to go!

689
46:10.851 --> 46:12.519
‎I saw pork cutlet on today's lunch menu.

690
46:13.437 --> 46:14.938
‎Does this mean I can't eat it?

691
46:15.981 --> 46:17.107
‎Jeez…

692
46:20.277 --> 46:22.404
‎Are you on your way to eat pork cutlet?

693
46:23.030 --> 46:25.741
‎If this means I can't check on Hyeon-a, ‎that's not good either.

694
46:27.034 --> 46:28.410
‎Come with me.

695
46:28.494 --> 46:30.621
‎I got fired, but you only got suspended.

696
46:31.121 --> 46:32.748
‎All right, wait up.

697
46:34.541 --> 46:36.001
‎We need to check on our patient.

698
47:33.141 --> 47:36.061
‎BONGBONG AUTO REPAIR SHOP

699
47:40.065 --> 47:41.358
‎11:30 A.M. ‎MONDAY, MAY 4

700
47:49.241 --> 47:51.159
‎SEMINAR ROOM

701
47:53.787 --> 47:55.914
‎We had such a good time ‎eating ‎tteokbokki‎ yesterday.

702
47:55.998 --> 47:56.832
‎Are they still talking?

703
47:57.416 --> 47:58.875
‎Do we go in when they call us?

704
47:58.959 --> 47:59.835
‎I'm not sure.

705
48:01.169 --> 48:02.963
‎-Is the meeting over? ‎-A while ago.

706
48:03.547 --> 48:04.840
‎They wrapped it up quickly.

707
48:04.923 --> 48:06.758
‎Then why did they call us?

708
48:08.677 --> 48:09.761
‎Man…

709
48:11.680 --> 48:15.559
‎Look who it is. ‎The heroes from yesterday's surgery.

710
48:16.143 --> 48:17.144
‎Take a seat.

711
48:29.698 --> 48:31.825
‎What on earth made you do that?

712
48:31.908 --> 48:34.244
‎If you won't give us a chance to explain,

713
48:34.745 --> 48:36.204
‎why did you call us here?

714
48:36.288 --> 48:38.665
‎We heard you were right outside,

715
48:38.749 --> 48:42.210
‎so it only seemed right ‎to tell you directly.

716
48:42.294 --> 48:43.962
‎The thing is,

717
48:44.630 --> 48:47.132
‎pushing through such a high-risk surgery

718
48:47.215 --> 48:50.886
‎created far too many chances ‎for something to go wrong.

719
48:50.969 --> 48:55.057
‎The IRB was already aware of the risks ‎involved in this surgery,

720
48:55.140 --> 48:57.517
‎which is why they kept ‎postponing the meeting.

721
48:58.101 --> 49:01.396
‎All the more reason to call a meeting ‎and discuss it sooner.

722
49:01.480 --> 49:04.274
‎And yet, you disregarded it ‎to proceed with the surgery

723
49:04.358 --> 49:05.942
‎and put the patient in danger.

724
49:06.443 --> 49:09.988
‎Bringing in unauthorized ‎outside medical personnel

725
49:10.072 --> 49:11.281
‎was also a major issue.

726
49:11.365 --> 49:13.408
‎She was there on my authority.

727
49:13.492 --> 49:15.160
‎We took that into account as well.

728
49:15.952 --> 49:18.914
‎You barely know that person.

729
49:19.539 --> 49:22.959
‎The OR is sacred. ‎How could you let just anyone come in?

730
49:23.043 --> 49:24.002
‎Unbelievable.

731
49:25.295 --> 49:29.466
‎We temporarily suspended you from duties ‎while we wait for the meeting's outcome,

732
49:29.549 --> 49:33.053
‎based on the reasonable suspicion ‎that this might happen again.

733
49:33.136 --> 49:36.181
‎But then I heard Dr. Kim took patients.

734
49:36.264 --> 49:39.518
‎Am I supposed to do nothing ‎when there's a critical patient?

735
49:39.601 --> 49:42.437
‎The hospital is short-staffed ‎because of the strike.

736
49:42.521 --> 49:45.482
‎If you suspend us for doing our job, ‎who's left to work?

737
49:45.565 --> 49:46.817
‎Dr. Jo Won-jin.

738
49:47.901 --> 49:53.281
‎You planned the surgery from the start ‎together with Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

739
49:53.365 --> 49:56.576
‎It looks like you had no intention ‎of not doing the surgery.

740
49:57.744 --> 49:59.246
‎The same goes for you, Dr. Park.

741
50:00.455 --> 50:01.665
‎Yes, sir.

742
50:01.748 --> 50:04.751
‎I don't regret taking part in the surgery.

743
50:06.753 --> 50:08.255
‎You don't regret it?

744
50:08.839 --> 50:10.966
‎Dr. Do and Dr. Bae.

745
50:11.049 --> 50:12.259
‎Is that how you feel too?

746
50:13.385 --> 50:15.929
‎What happened yesterday ‎was an emergency situation.

747
50:16.513 --> 50:19.933
‎We had no other option. ‎We only did it out of desperation.

748
50:20.684 --> 50:24.521
‎We will face whatever the outcome is.

749
50:24.604 --> 50:27.607
‎But please consider ‎that a child's life was on the line--

750
50:27.691 --> 50:29.776
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon, ‎relieved of position.

751
50:30.485 --> 50:33.155
‎Dr. Do Yun-sik, ‎two-month disciplinary suspension.

752
50:33.238 --> 50:35.532
‎Dr. Bae Heung-gon, ‎one-month disciplinary suspension.

753
50:35.615 --> 50:37.784
‎Dr. Jo Won-jin, ‎three-month disciplinary suspension.

754
50:37.868 --> 50:40.203
‎Dr. Kim Seong-jin, ‎one-month disciplinary suspension.

755
50:40.287 --> 50:42.414
‎Dr. Park Tae-gyeong, ‎two-month disciplinary suspension.

756
50:42.497 --> 50:44.916
‎-And-- ‎-Dr. Park is an intern.

757
50:45.000 --> 50:47.043
‎Two months is severe disciplinary action.

758
50:47.127 --> 50:50.338
‎That's absolutely unfair to an intern ‎who only has a year

759
50:50.422 --> 50:52.257
‎to complete his department rotations.

760
50:52.340 --> 50:53.341
‎Gye Su-jeong.

761
50:57.137 --> 50:58.388
‎Contract termination remains in effect.

762
51:02.017 --> 51:04.311
‎If something goes wrong…

763
51:04.853 --> 51:06.980
‎If something happens to that kid--

764
51:07.063 --> 51:08.148
‎Hyeon-a.

765
51:10.901 --> 51:11.818
‎Lee Hyeon-a.

766
51:12.986 --> 51:14.738
‎Patient outcome aside,

767
51:14.821 --> 51:18.033
‎this comes down to ‎the ethics of medical practice.

768
51:18.116 --> 51:21.745
‎Is putting the patient's life on the line ‎with a reckless surgery

769
51:21.828 --> 51:25.499
‎solely and purely ‎in the patient's best interest?

770
51:25.582 --> 51:27.793
‎That was our main focus.

771
51:29.336 --> 51:30.462
‎Most importantly,

772
51:31.087 --> 51:33.840
‎we're wrapping this up ‎before health authorities investigate,

773
51:33.924 --> 51:35.258
‎so just accept the consequences.

774
51:35.884 --> 51:38.845
‎The med school quota issue ‎and strike are bad enough.

775
51:38.929 --> 51:41.848
‎Let's end it here ‎before they pick us apart.

776
51:46.937 --> 51:48.021
‎Oh, right.

777
51:48.104 --> 51:50.023
‎Bu Seung-gwon… I mean, Dr. Bu.

778
51:50.106 --> 51:51.983
‎Why don't you try ‎that door in your office today?

779
51:52.609 --> 51:53.610
‎It's your last day there,

780
51:53.693 --> 51:56.404
‎so you might as well try it out.

781
52:01.785 --> 52:02.619
‎What's this?

782
52:03.370 --> 52:05.247
‎Is the meeting over already?

783
52:05.747 --> 52:08.291
‎That's a shame. ‎I was looking forward to it.

784
52:08.834 --> 52:10.168
‎-And you are? ‎-Oh.

785
52:10.252 --> 52:13.046
‎Hello, I'm Jang Hui-suk.

786
52:14.714 --> 52:16.508
‎Oh, the melon lady.

787
52:17.634 --> 52:21.054
‎If you want some melon ‎or if you're looking for a job,

788
52:21.137 --> 52:23.223
‎hold onto my business card.

789
52:25.767 --> 52:28.770
‎Oh, and this is Ms. Lee Hyeon-a's mother.

790
52:29.271 --> 52:31.648
‎Goodness, hello.

791
52:32.899 --> 52:34.568
‎-Let's get going. ‎-Yes, sir.

792
52:34.651 --> 52:35.527
‎Excuse me.

793
52:36.528 --> 52:38.154
‎Has the disciplinary action been decided?

794
52:38.238 --> 52:39.322
‎Ma'am.

795
52:39.948 --> 52:42.409
‎It must have been so stressful for you.

796
52:42.492 --> 52:44.160
‎Disciplinary action has been finalized.

797
52:44.244 --> 52:45.954
‎Just focus on your child now.

798
52:46.580 --> 52:48.623
‎We're busy, so please excuse us.

799
52:48.707 --> 52:51.001
‎My child's surgery yesterday

800
52:51.084 --> 52:53.169
‎was dangerous ‎and shouldn't have been attempted.

801
52:53.962 --> 52:55.755
‎Is that what today's decision means?

802
52:56.506 --> 52:58.550
‎Yes, that's basically it.

803
52:58.633 --> 53:00.260
‎Then I would like to sue.

804
53:10.228 --> 53:14.858
‎I'd like to sue the primary surgeon ‎and everyone else who was in the OR.

805
53:19.070 --> 53:20.280
‎Of course.

806
53:20.363 --> 53:23.533
‎We won't stop you ‎from taking legal action.

807
53:23.617 --> 53:26.870
‎The IRB's opinion carries legal weight.

808
53:26.953 --> 53:29.080
‎We can provide the materials whenever--

809
53:29.164 --> 53:32.959
‎I'm suing Guseo University Medical Center ‎and the Guseo Foundation as well.

810
53:34.794 --> 53:36.421
‎We were at the main hospital at first.

811
53:36.922 --> 53:39.841
‎But they sent us here, ‎saying there were no other options.

812
53:40.634 --> 53:43.595
‎It felt like they just dumped us here.

813
53:44.471 --> 53:47.766
‎If the main hospital ‎hadn't recklessly sent us here,

814
53:47.849 --> 53:50.060
‎my child wouldn't have had that surgery.

815
53:51.436 --> 53:54.522
‎Ma'am, let's discuss this later--

816
53:54.606 --> 53:55.607
‎Also,

817
53:55.690 --> 53:58.902
‎I'm suing the hospital's foundation ‎for hiring the doctor

818
53:58.985 --> 54:00.362
‎who performed such a risky surgery.

819
54:01.196 --> 54:03.239
‎I'm going to sue all parties involved.

820
54:03.323 --> 54:05.575
‎Today's disciplinary action ‎is proof of liability, right?

821
54:10.205 --> 54:12.666
‎Why would I sue Dr. Gye?

822
54:12.749 --> 54:15.835
‎She's the only doctor who treated Hyeon-a.

823
54:17.003 --> 54:18.546
‎Not just her. Everyone.

824
54:19.297 --> 54:22.050
‎Tell them you'll sue the hospital ‎and the foundation behind it.

825
54:23.343 --> 54:24.386
‎Me?

826
54:24.469 --> 54:27.639
‎That way, Dr. Gye can ‎continue to work here

827
54:28.431 --> 54:30.684
‎and monitor Hyeon-a.

828
54:31.977 --> 54:35.438
‎Ma'am, I understand your frustration,

829
54:36.648 --> 54:39.609
‎but there's no point. ‎It's like throwing eggs at a boulder.

830
54:39.693 --> 54:41.361
‎Patients always lose in these lawsuits--

831
54:41.444 --> 54:43.905
‎You don't throw eggs to break a boulder.

832
54:44.656 --> 54:45.532
‎What?

833
54:46.533 --> 54:49.869
‎You want the egg splatter to leave a mark.

834
54:51.079 --> 54:54.082
‎You want it to rot and reek ‎as time goes by

835
54:54.791 --> 54:56.584
‎so it never washes off.

836
54:57.377 --> 54:58.211
‎Dr. Gye.

837
54:58.294 --> 55:00.046
‎No one will wash it off.

838
55:00.755 --> 55:03.383
‎And more eggs will get thrown at it.

839
55:03.466 --> 55:05.969
‎Then people will point at it and say…

840
55:07.971 --> 55:08.930
‎"This is it."

841
55:10.765 --> 55:12.183
‎"This is the place that reeks."

842
55:18.690 --> 55:21.484
‎They put the disciplinary action on hold.

843
55:21.568 --> 55:22.444
‎Thank you.

844
55:23.611 --> 55:25.488
‎But it's just on hold, not dropped.

845
55:26.406 --> 55:28.742
‎They're just trying to save face.

846
55:28.825 --> 55:29.868
‎Don't worry about it.

847
55:32.912 --> 55:33.913
‎Thank you.

848
55:35.832 --> 55:36.791
‎Not at all.

849
55:37.792 --> 55:40.086
‎You saved my daughter, Dr. Gye.

850
55:40.962 --> 55:42.047
‎I had to return the favor.

851
55:44.632 --> 55:45.592
‎I should go now.

852
55:50.805 --> 55:51.639
‎One more thing.

853
55:52.432 --> 55:53.767
‎Dr. Gye.

854
55:54.267 --> 55:55.435
‎Yes?

855
55:55.518 --> 55:58.188
‎Can you say it to me again?

856
55:59.522 --> 56:01.858
‎I know it might not be enough

857
56:02.650 --> 56:05.779
‎after everything Hyeon-a has been through…

858
56:06.529 --> 56:07.655
‎But still…

859
56:07.739 --> 56:10.325
‎I don't ever…

860
56:12.410 --> 56:13.578
‎fail.

861
56:19.793 --> 56:20.668
‎Thank you.

862
56:28.134 --> 56:29.302
‎LEE HYEON-A, F/8

863
56:30.386 --> 56:34.349
‎PRIMARY PHYSICIAN: GYE SU-JEONG

864
56:34.432 --> 56:35.600
‎MAIN BUILDING WALL CONSTRUCTION

865
56:35.683 --> 56:37.310
‎I was only suspended for a day,

866
56:37.393 --> 56:39.979
‎but it made me appreciate my job more.

867
56:40.063 --> 56:43.274
‎-That's how I feel. ‎-But you actually took in patients.

868
56:43.358 --> 56:45.902
‎The firefighter and most of them are okay.

869
56:45.985 --> 56:47.362
‎But one is brain dead.

870
56:48.488 --> 56:50.240
‎They're an organ donor,

871
56:50.323 --> 56:51.574
‎and the family already knows,

872
56:52.158 --> 56:55.537
‎so the transplant coordinator ‎has been making calls.

873
56:58.665 --> 57:00.834
‎If they can afford ‎to put something like this up,

874
57:00.917 --> 57:04.003
‎they ought to finish ‎the construction instead.

875
57:07.257 --> 57:08.258
‎Are you guys staying?

876
57:09.467 --> 57:10.677
‎Well, see you.

877
57:23.440 --> 57:24.649
‎"Gu Yeo-rim."

878
57:24.732 --> 57:28.194
‎"First director of Guseo Medical Center."

879
57:28.278 --> 57:29.654
‎"Prede…"

880
57:30.238 --> 57:31.573
‎"Prede…"

881
57:31.656 --> 57:33.032
‎"Predecessor

882
57:33.116 --> 57:34.701
‎of Guseo University Medical Center."

883
57:34.784 --> 57:37.829
‎-"A pio…" ‎-"A pioneer."

884
57:37.912 --> 57:40.457
‎"A pioneer for women in…"

885
57:40.540 --> 57:41.416
‎"Medicine."

886
57:41.499 --> 57:43.251
‎"She led the expansion

887
57:43.918 --> 57:45.420
‎of gynecological care."

888
57:45.503 --> 57:47.422
‎Keep reading.

889
57:48.548 --> 57:50.550
‎I learned how to say this in Korean.

890
57:51.176 --> 57:52.802
‎Chukhahamnida.

891
57:52.886 --> 57:55.889
‎It's been a real privilege ‎to work with a surgeon like you.

892
57:56.890 --> 57:59.184
‎Now you're going back home ‎to receive a new heart.

893
58:00.059 --> 58:02.061
‎Congratulations. I truly mean it.

894
58:12.739 --> 58:13.740
‎-Really? ‎-Yes.

895
58:13.823 --> 58:15.450
‎Wait, that means…

896
58:15.533 --> 58:17.577
‎He's coming here to get a transplant.

897
58:19.829 --> 58:21.664
‎We get to see him in person?

898
58:21.748 --> 58:24.167
‎But why come here of all places?

899
58:24.250 --> 58:25.793
‎Why not somewhere else?

900
58:25.877 --> 58:29.088
‎What do you mean? ‎What's wrong with our hospital?

901
58:39.265 --> 58:40.099
‎What's wrong?

902
58:40.183 --> 58:41.309
‎What is it?

903
58:42.018 --> 58:44.521
‎What's going on? ‎Did something happen to Su-jeong?

904
59:10.547 --> 59:12.090
‎Who's this man?

905
59:13.132 --> 59:14.217
‎"Kim Seung-hyo."

906
59:14.300 --> 59:17.679
‎"A graduate of Guseo University ‎and a surgeon who founded

907
59:17.762 --> 59:21.933
‎the medical volunteer organization, ‎White Wings Medical Corps."

908
59:22.016 --> 59:27.522
‎"He provided humanitarian care ‎and medical aid in impoverished countries,

909
59:27.605 --> 59:29.524
‎earning him a Nobel Prize nomination."

910
59:30.024 --> 59:32.986
‎"Saving countless children ‎with his exceptional skill,

911
59:33.069 --> 59:35.196
‎he is revered as a true physician ‎of our time

912
59:35.280 --> 59:37.991
‎with a golden heart and the hands of God."

913
59:39.701 --> 59:40.702
‎Let's go now.

914
59:41.619 --> 59:43.621
‎You read so well, Ga-eul.

915
59:46.916 --> 59:50.295
‎KIM SEUNG-HYO ‎FOUNDER OF WHITE WINGS MEDICAL CORPS

916
59:57.093 --> 01:00:01.097
‎Why does he insist on ‎having surgery at this hospital?

917
01:00:01.180 --> 01:00:02.932
‎Doesn't he have limited mobility?

918
01:00:03.016 --> 01:00:05.977
‎He says both his guardian ‎and the surgeon he wants

919
01:00:06.060 --> 01:00:07.729
‎are at our hospital.

920
01:00:07.812 --> 01:00:09.480
‎Who's the guardian?

921
01:00:09.981 --> 01:00:14.861
‎PROUD FIGURES OF GUSEO

922
01:00:38.593 --> 01:00:40.595
‎It's Dr. Jo Won-jin.

923
01:00:42.347 --> 01:00:44.682
‎Dr. Jo Won-jin?

924
01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:46.643
‎Then who's the surgeon?

925
01:00:47.518 --> 01:00:50.772
‎The one who performed ‎his first transplant.

926
01:00:57.320 --> 01:00:58.613
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

927
01:01:02.867 --> 01:01:03.785
‎Aunt.

928
01:01:04.911 --> 01:01:07.914
‎Aunt, wake up!

929
01:01:08.998 --> 01:01:09.916
‎Aunt!

930
01:01:58.297 --> 01:02:00.299
‎TWO DAYS LATER

931
01:02:00.925 --> 01:02:04.595
‎PATIENT: KIM SEUNG-HYO ‎PRIMARY SURGEON: GYE SU-JEONG

932
01:02:22.321 --> 01:02:24.741
‎PATIENT: KIM SEUNG-HYO ‎PRIMARY SURGEON: GYE SU-JEONG

933
01:02:59.192 --> 01:03:00.067
‎Park Tae-gyeong.

934
01:03:02.195 --> 01:03:03.070
‎Park Tae-gyeong!

935
01:03:27.887 --> 01:03:29.847
‎It's been a long time…

936
01:03:33.392 --> 01:03:35.520
‎Doctor X.

937
01:03:48.616 --> 01:03:51.577
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

938
01:04:30.700 --> 01:04:33.661
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

939
01:04:34.245 --> 01:04:35.621
‎It's been a long time, sir.

940
01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:37.498
‎I just stood there watching.

941
01:04:38.082 --> 01:04:40.126
‎But Dr. Gye saved his life again.

942
01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:43.004
‎I heard Dr. Kim Seung-hyo ‎personally requested Gye Su-jeong.

943
01:04:43.087 --> 01:04:45.047
‎Who on earth is Gye Su-jeong?

944
01:04:45.131 --> 01:04:47.258
‎She said he told her to come.

945
01:04:47.341 --> 01:04:49.677
‎All of the children I met back then…

946
01:04:50.469 --> 01:04:52.680
‎Dad is a monster.

947
01:04:52.763 --> 01:04:54.432
‎I need you to get up here right now!

948
01:04:55.016 --> 01:04:55.892
‎Dr. Gye.

949
01:04:55.975 --> 01:04:58.227
‎Please. Just this once.

950
01:04:58.311 --> 01:05:00.271
‎Could you please fail?

951
01:05:00.938 --> 01:05:05.818
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
